    "https://www.martyncurrey.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/zs-040-BreakoutBoard_1200-584x607.jpg",
    "https://www.martyncurrey.com/arduino-with-hc-05-bluetooth-module-at-mode/"
  ],
  "priceUsd": 4,
  "supplierQuery": "HC-05 ZS-040 Bluetooth serial module 6 pin",
  "footprint": "Connector_PinHeader_2.54mm:PinHeader_1x06_P2.54mm_Vertical",
  "buildNotes": [
    "Power VCC from 5 V (VIN/VBUS): the ZS-040 board's regulator needs at least 3.6 V, so the 3.3 V pin is not enough.",
    "RXD and TXD are 3.3 V logic. ESP32 and Pico connect directly (cross over: board TX to RXD, board RX to TXD); from a 5 V Arduino put a 1k/2k divider on RXD.",
    "AT mode: hold the little button (or tie EN to 3.3 V) while powering the module up; the LED blinks slowly (about every 2 s) and the module answers AT commands at 38400 baud, 8N1. Every command ends with \\r\\n.",
    "In normal data mode (LED blinking fast) AT commands are not answered: the module just passes bytes to the paired phone, at the data baud (AT+UART?, often 9600 on ZS-040 boards).",
    "Default pairing PIN is 1234 (some firmware: 0000). STATE goes high while a phone is connected."
  ],
